  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Dr.R.Kathiravan vs The State Of Tamil Nadu on 11 December, 2017 Author: T.Raja Bench: T.Raja In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated : 11.12.2017 Coram The Honourable Mr.Justice T.Raja W.P.No.31957 of 2017 01. Dr.R.Kathiravan 02. Dr.A.Ramakrishnan 03. Dr.S.Mariappan 04. Dr.R.Ramesh Babu 05. Dr.T.Anuradha 06. Dr.K.Tamilselvan 07. Dr.M.Kavikumar 08. Dr.J.Venkatesh 09. Dr.V.Senthilkumar 10. Dr.N.Dhakshinamoorthy 11. Dr.M.Jegadish Chandra Bose 12. Dr.G.Selvaraj 13. Dr.V.Senthilkumar 14. Dr.T.Kalaivani 15. Dr.A.Pushparaj 16. Dr.G.Varalakshmi 17. Dr.R.Karunakaran 18. Dr.B.Suguna 19. Dr.R.V.Ravi .. Petitioners -vs- 1. The State of Tamil Nadu rep.by its Principal Secretary to Government Health & Family Welfare Department Secretariat, Fort St.George Chennai 600 009 2. The Commissioner of Food Safety Tamil Nadu Food Safety & Drugs Administration Department Dr.R.Kathiravan vs The State Of Tamil Nadu on 11 December, 2017 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/194955548/ 1 Anna Salai, Dms Compound Teynampet Chennai 600 006 .. Respondents Petition under Article 226 of the Constitution of India, praying for the issue of a Writ For Petitioners :: Mr.A.L.Somayaji Senior Counsel for Mr.G.Sankaran For Respondents :: Mr.V.Jayaprakash Narayanan Special Government Pleader Order This writ petition has been filed seeking a mandamus, forbearing the respondents from reverting the petitioners from the post of Designated Officer in the name of repatriation to former service in violation of condition of service of the petitioners and consequently directing the respondents to pass orders for fixation of pay of the petitioners in the post of Designated Officer in the scale of pay of Rs.15600-39100+5700 GP as sanctioned in G.O.Ms.No.347 Health and Family Welfare (AB2) Department dated 22.12.2011 from the date of their initial appointment, on permanent absorption of petitioners in the post of Designated Officer in Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drugs Administration Department with all consequential and other attendant benefits, within a time frame to be fixed by this Hon'ble Court.",
    "facts": "Order This writ petition has been filed seeking a mandamus, forbearing the respondents from reverting the petitioners from the post of Designated Officer in the name of repatriation to former service in violation of condition of service of the petitioners and consequently directing the respondents to pass orders for fixation of pay of the petitioners in the post of Designated Officer in the scale of pay of Rs.15600-39100+5700 GP as sanctioned in G.O.Ms.No.347 Health and Family Welfare (AB2) Department dated 22.12.2011 from the date of their initial appointment, on permanent absorption of petitioners in the post of Designated Officer in Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drugs Administration Department with all consequential and other attendant benefits, within a time frame to be fixed by this Hon'ble Court. Pursuant thereto, the Commissioner of Food Safety and Drug Administration, in his letter dated 21.11.2014, to the Secretary to Government, Health and Family Welfare Department, Chennai, has requested to fix their pay to the post of Designated Officer. Now that the proposal is pending, there is an apprehension on the part of the petitioners that they may be sent back to the parent department as Health Officers in the Tamil Nadu Public Health Department, which cannot be done.",
